ords $N$, a configuration $\theta$ of the generator produces a synthetic dataset $G_\theta$. The goal is to find a configuration whose dataset belongs to the set $\mathcal{F}(S,N)$ of datasets with exactly $N$ records that conform to $S$ and that maximizes the gain in classifier performance $\Delta U$, while keeping the distance from the real distribution $L_{\mathrm{fid}}$, the privacy risk $L_{\mathrm{priv}}$ and the cost $\kappa$ low:
+\begin{equation}
+\theta^{\star}\in\operatorname*{arg\,min}_{\theta:\,G_{\theta}\in\mathcal{F}(S,N)}
+\bigl(-\Delta U,\;L_{\mathrm{fid}},\;L_{\mathrm{priv}},\;\kappa\bigr)(\theta).
+\label{eq:multiobjective}
+\end{equation}
+The constraint follows the data-quality dimensions of completeness and conformity~\cite{wang1996beyond,batini2009methodologies}, and the objectives are the utility, fidelity and privacy on which synthetic data are evaluated~\cite{qian2023synthcity,lautrup2025syntheval}, together with cost.
 
