+The control layer applies to generation a principle long used in data management: data produced by an automatic process are checked against explicit constraints before they are accepted. Kamino enforces integrity constraints during private data synthesis~\cite{ge2021kamino}, data-cleaning systems combine statistical inference with integrity constraints~\cite{chu2013holistic,qin2024bclean}, and recovering structured records from the free-form output of an LLM has been studied as a data-engineering problem~\cite{rorseth2026recovering}. In \system, the constraints are the columns and types inferred from the real data, and the checks are applied to every response of the LLM, in the action--observation loop of LLM agents~\cite{yao2023react,wang2024agentsurvey}.
